# Netlify redirect rules (evaluated top-down; real files are always served
# first, so these only fire for paths with no matching file).
#
# 1) Asset guard: a MISSING file under /assets/ (e.g. a stale hashed chunk
#    referenced by a cached shell, or an asset still propagating right after a
#    deploy) must return a real 404 — NOT the HTML shell. Returning HTML for a
#    module script triggers "Failed to load module script … MIME type text/html"
#    and a blank screen. This rule keeps such requests honest.
/assets/*   /assets/:splat   404
/sw.js      /sw.js           404

# 2) SPA fallback: any other non-file path — a bookmarked/shared deep link like
#    /present or /present/<slug> that lost its "#/" — is served the app shell
#    (200, no redirect) instead of Netlify's branded 404. The shim in index.html
#    then moves that path into the hash route.
/*          /index.html      200
